# Overlay example: production-quality-ownership

Drop this file at `<consumer>/.claude/skills/production-quality-ownership/SKILL.md.local`.
It is APPENDED to the plugin's SKILL.md at runtime (extend-only — never replaces plugin behavior).

The plugin's generic skill covers the 7-question framework. This overlay injects the product-specific surfaces that Q5 ("every system surface this could affect") needs to be useful. Replace the example below with your product's actual cross-coupling map.

---

## <product> cross-coupling map

When a new field lands on the primary form, the typical surfaces are:

1. `lib/validation/<schema>.ts` — validation schema (Zod / equivalent)
2. `lib/db/<schema>.ts` — DB column (Drizzle / Prisma / SQL migration)
3. `<snapshot>` JSONB shape — captured at submission
4. Backfill SQL for unconfirmed rows (confirmed rows are usually immutable)
5. Each role's view page that displays this data
6. Each notification recipient's email template (HTML + plaintext + all configured locales)
7. Public-API serializer (pass through the privacy/GDPR filter if applicable)
8. i18n keys for every configured locale
9. User-facing docs (`docs/...md`)
10. RAG / chatbot knowledge base copies (if your project maintains them)
11. Review-summary component on the submission page
12. Integration test + E2E spec
13. Architecture / decisions doc (if the change is interpretive)

## Regulatory context

If the product is in a regulated domain (e.g. EU Reg 2024/900 + 2025/1410, GDPR, HIPAA, financial), document the rule citations the agent must trace decisions back to:

- Rule citation + URL
- Where in the codebase the rule is enforced
- Where "exception" decisions live (e.g. `docs/founder-decisions.md`)

## Stakeholder-facing voice

Q7 ("a regulator/auditor reads this commit + PR description") needs project-specific stakeholders named:

- Who reads commit messages? (legal team, board, regulators, external partners)
- What's the audit cadence (quarterly review, on-demand subpoena, etc.)?
- Where does the "why" trail live when not in the commit message?
